<section class="dark" id="specs"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">0.1</div><h2>Spec sheet<span>By the numbers</span></h2><p class="intro">The essentials on one page. The rest of the manual shows you how to make the most of each number.</p></div>
  <div class="metrics">
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ RGB pads, polyphonic aftertouch</span><b>16</b></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ Stereo voices</span><b>32</b></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ Pad banks</span><b>A–H</b></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ Effect types, 4 engines</span><b>60</b></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ Battery life</span><b>~5 h</b></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">↓ Internal storage</span><b>8 GB</b></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ports">
      <span class="lbl">↓ Connections</span>
      <ul>
        <li>Line In<span>1/4" TRS</span></li>
        <li>Line Out<span>1/4" TRS</span></li>
        <li>Headphones<span>1/8"</span></li>
        <li>MIDI In/Out<span>1/8" TRS*</span></li>
        <li>Sync Out<span>Clock</span></li>
        <li>USB-C<span>Power</span></li>
        <li>MicroSD<span>Expansion</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lbl" style="margin-top:14px">* Needs a TRS-to-MIDI DIN adapter, not included. About 2 GB of the 8 GB hold factory content.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<main>
<section id="start"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">1.0</div><h2>The first hour<span>Eight steps</span></h2><p class="intro">Do these once, in order. After that the machine stops feeling strange. Your checkmarks are saved in this browser.</p></div>
  <div class="indent"><ul class="check">
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c1" aria-labelledby="en-c1t"><b id="en-c1t">Charge the battery over USB-C</b><p>About 5 hours away from the wall. You can play while it charges.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c2" aria-labelledby="en-c2t"><b id="en-c2t">Update the firmware</b><p>On akaipro.com, MPC Sample page. Several features and fixes arrived after launch; this guide assumes version 1.3.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c3" aria-labelledby="en-c3t"><b id="en-c3t">Headphones on, <span class="key">MAIN VOLUME</span> down</b><p>The built-in speaker is for sketching. You only hear the low end on headphones or monitors.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c4" aria-labelledby="en-c4t"><b id="en-c4t">Play a factory kit</b><p>There are over 100. Load one, press <span class="key">▶</span> and play along. The pads respond to velocity and pressure.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c5" aria-labelledby="en-c5t"><b id="en-c5t">Step through banks with <span class="key">PAD BANK</span></b><p>Each bank, A through H, is another 16 pads. The screen shows which bank you’re on.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c6" aria-labelledby="en-c6t"><b id="en-c6t">Mute with <span class="key pp">MUTE</span></b><p>While the music plays, hold MUTE and tap pads. <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + MUTE brings everything back.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c7" aria-labelledby="en-c7t"><b id="en-c7t">Record your first sound</b><p><span class="key rec">SMP REC</span>, talk into the built-in mic, SMP REC again. You now have a sample on a pad. See recipe 4.2.</p></li>
    <li><input type="checkbox" id="en-c8" aria-labelledby="en-c8t"><b id="en-c8t">Undo without fear</b><p><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">−</span> is Undo, <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">+</span> is Redo.</p></li>
  </ul></div>
</div></section>

<section id="anatomy" class="anat"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">2.0</div><h2>Anatomy<span>of the panel</span></h2><p class="intro">Tap a number to see what it does. Almost every button has a second function, printed in gray underneath: hold <span class="key">SHIFT</span> to use it.</p></div>
  <div class="anatomy">
    <div class="panel-fig">
      {{DEVICE_FLAT}}
      <div class="figcap"><span class="lbl">↓ Top view, 24 controls</span><div class="toggle"><span class="lbl shiftHint">Secondary functions</span><button type="button" class="shiftBtn" aria-pressed="false">Shift</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="partsWrap"><ul class="parts"></ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="concepts"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">3.0</div><h2>How the MPC thinks<span>Four layers</span></h2><p class="intro">One inside the other. Once this clicks, the menus make sense.</p></div>
  <div class="concept">
    <div class="fig">{{LAYERS}}</div>
    <div class="defs">
      <div><span class="lbl">↓ 3.1</span><b>Sample</b><p>An audio file. A kick, a piano phrase, your voice, a Lisbon streetcar.</p></div>
      <div><span class="lbl">↓ 3.2</span><b>Pad</b><p>Where the sample lives, with its own rules: start and end, Loop, Reverse, level, tuning.</p></div>
      <div><span class="lbl">↓ 3.3</span><b>Sequence</b><p>A recorded pattern of pad hits, with a length in bars. Think of it as a section: intro, verse, chorus.</p></div>
      <div><span class="lbl">↓ 3.4</span><b>Project</b><p>Everything together: samples, pads, sequences, tempo. It’s what you save and open again.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="indent"><p class="note">The buttons on the left choose the <b>mode</b>: <span class="key">SAMPLE</span> to record and edit sounds, <span class="key">SEQ</span> to compose, <span class="key fx">PAD FX</span> and <span class="key fx">KNOB FX</span> for effects. Knobs K1–K3 and the B1–B3 buttons above the screen change job with each mode, so always read the screen to see what they control right now.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="recipes"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">4.0</div><h2>Recipes<span>Seven tasks</span></h2><p class="intro">In the order you’ll need them. Each takes 10 to 30 minutes.</p></div>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.1</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Record a beat with a factory kit</h3><p class="why">The classic MPC move: play live over a metronome and let quantize tidy up.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span>Press <span class="key">SEQ</span>. Set the length with <b>K1</b> (start with 2 bars).</span></li>
      <li><span>Tap the tempo on <span class="key">TAP TEMPO</span>. <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + TAP TEMPO turns on the metronome.</span></li>
      <li><span>Turn on Record Quantize with <b>B3</b> and pick the grid with <b>K2</b>. 1/16 is a good start.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key pad">PAD 4</span> turns on the Count-in.</span></li>
      <li><span>Hit <span class="key rec">SEQ REC</span> and play just the kick. When the sequence loops, recording continues as overdub: add the snare, then the hats.</span></li>
      <li><span>Made a mistake? Hold <span class="key">ERASE</span> and the pad during playback and that pad’s notes disappear.</span></li>
      <li><span>Press <span class="key rec">SEQ REC</span> again to stop recording without stopping the music.</span></li>
    </ol></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.2</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Sample anything</h3><p class="why">The built-in mic turns the world into a sound library. For records or synths, use the line input.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">SAMPLE</span> (Input Config) picks the source: built-in mic or Line In.</span></li>
      <li><span>Press <span class="key rec">SMP REC</span> and set the <b>threshold</b> with <b>K3</b>. Recording only starts once the sound crosses this level; the waveform icon lights up when it does.</span></li>
      <li><span>Pick the target pad, make the sound, press SMP REC again.</span></li>
      <li><span>In <span class="key">SAMPLE</span>, trim start and end with the knobs.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">SMP SELECT</span> (Save Sample) stores it as a file.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="tip"><span class="lbl">↓ Recall</span>Played something great without recording? <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key rec">SMP REC</span> or <span class="key rec">SEQ REC</span> brings back what just happened.</div></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.3</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Chop a loop across 16 pads</h3><p class="why">The “chop”: a record phrase cut into pieces and rearranged with your fingers.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span>Select the pad with the sample and press <span class="key pp">CHOP</span>.</span></li>
      <li><span>Choose the mode with <b>K3</b>: <b>Threshold</b> cuts at transients (drums), <b>Regions 4/8/16</b> splits into equal parts (loops in time), <b>Manual</b> lets you mark cuts by ear.</span></li>
      <li><span>The pads now play each slice. Play them in a different order.</span></li>
      <li><span>Record a sequence with the slices (recipe 4.1).</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="tip"><span class="lbl">↓ Trick</span>On a one-bar loop in 4/4, Regions 16 gives you exactly one slice per sixteenth note.</div></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.4</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Note Repeat, swing and dynamics</h3><p class="why">Rolling hi-hats and snare rolls without a drummer’s hands.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span>Hold <span class="key">NOTE REPEAT</span> and a pad: the sound repeats at the division set with B1–B3.</span></li>
      <li><span>Press harder or softer on the pad: aftertouch changes the intensity.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + NOTE REPEAT switches to triplets.</span></li>
      <li><span>Set swing on the sequencer screen. 54% to 58% is the classic groove.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key pad">PAD 1</span> (Full Level) plays every pad at max velocity.</span></li>
    </ol></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.5</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Arrange: double, halve, copy</h3><p class="why">From a loop to a structure.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key pad">PAD 3</span> (Double Seq) doubles the sequence. Record variations in the second half.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key pad">PAD 2</span> (Half Seq) cuts it in half.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">ERASE</span> (Copy) copies a sequence so you can build new sections.</span></li>
      <li><span>Switch sequences during playback to arrange the track live.</span></li>
      <li><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key">SEQ</span> (Step Edit) shows notes one by one; here the fader nudges each event’s timing.</span></li>
    </ol></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.6</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Play melodies with 16 Levels</h3><p class="why">One sample spread across 16 pads, each at a different pitch.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span>Pick a short, pitched sample: a piano note, bass or voice.</span></li>
      <li><span>Press <span class="key pp">16 LEVELS</span>. <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + 16 LEVELS (Type) chooses which parameter changes.</span></li>
      <li><span>Set to tune, the pads become a 16-semitone keyboard.</span></li>
      <li><span>Press 16 LEVELS again to return to normal pads.</span></li>
    </ol></div>
  </article>

  <article class="recipe"><div class="big">4.7</div>
    <div class="head"><h3>Resample and save</h3><p class="why">Print the result, effects included, into a new sample.</p></div>
    <div class="body"><span class="lbl">↓ Steps</span><ol class="steps">
      <li><span>With the sequence ready, go to <span class="key rec">SMP REC</span> and choose <b>Resample</b> (Pad 11 on the record screen).</span></li>
      <li><span>The MPC records its own output to a new pad, effects and all.</span></li>
      <li><span>Chop, reverse or run that result through more effects.</span></li>
      <li><span>Save the project at the end of every session. Use microSD for backups.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="tip"><span class="lbl">↓ Fader</span>By default it controls pad level. <span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> + <span class="key pad">PAD 9</span> assigns another parameter, such as pitch or filter.</div></div>
  </article>
</div></section>

<section id="effects"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">5.0</div><h2>Effects<span>Four engines</span></h2><p class="intro">Two to play with your fingers, one to turn and one to glue it all. Record the music clean first and the effects after, in an overdub or a resample.</p></div>
  <div class="fxgrid">
    <div class="fx"><div class="big">1</div><h3>Pad FX</h3><p class="sub">Effects on the pads</p><span class="key fx">PAD FX</span><span class="lbl">↓ Includes</span><ul><li>16 effects, one per pad</li><li>Velocity-sensitive</li><li>Filters and beat repeat</li><li>Stutter, reverse, delay</li><li>Ring mod, lo-fi, granular</li></ul></div>
    <div class="fx"><div class="big">2</div><h3>Flex Beat</h3><p class="sub">Bend time</p><span class="key fx">SHIFT · PAD FX</span><span class="lbl">↓ Includes</span><ul><li>16 time-based effects</li><li>DJ scratches</li><li>Beat chops</li><li>Trance gate</li><li>Pitch and volume warps</li></ul></div>
    <div class="fx"><div class="big">3</div><h3>Knob FX</h3><p class="sub">One effect on the knobs</p><span class="key fx">KNOB FX</span><span class="lbl">↓ Includes</span><ul><li>Delays and reverbs</li><li>Amp simulation</li><li>Modulation</li><li>Vintage emulations</li><li>Shift + Knob FX: choose</li></ul></div>
    <div class="fx"><div class="big">4</div><h3>Color Compressor</h3><p class="sub">Glue on the output</p><span class="key sh">MASTER</span><span class="lbl">↓ Includes</span><ul><li>Retro-colored compression</li><li>Classic MPC density</li><li>Vinyl emulation</li><li>Tape emulation</li><li>Applies to everything</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="musicians"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">6.0</div><h2>For musicians<span>Translation</span></h2><p class="intro">You have the ear and the theory. What changes on the MPC is the vocabulary and thinking in a grid.</p></div>
  <div class="indent"><div class="tbl"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>You know…</th><th>On the MPC it’s</th><th>Tip</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Meter and subdivision</td><td>Bars + Q (quantize)</td><td>1/16 for hip-hop and house, 1/8 with Triplet for shuffle and 6/8.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Groove</td><td>Swing</td><td>Set it before recording hats; 54–58% sounds human.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Dynamics</td><td>Velocity + aftertouch</td><td>Turn off Full Level for snare ghost notes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Key</td><td>16 Levels (Tune)</td><td>Tune the sample to the root before spreading it across the pads.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Form</td><td>Sequences</td><td>One sequence per section. Copy + changes = variation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Harmony</td><td>Chord samples</td><td>Record chords from your instrument, one per pad, at project tempo.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Improvising</td><td>Recall</td><td>Play freely; Recall keeps what you just did.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div></div>
</div></section>

<section id="plan"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">7.0</div><h2>Plan<span>Four weeks</span></h2><p class="intro">Three short sessions a week, 20 to 40 minutes. End every session by saving something, even if it’s rough.</p></div>
  <div class="weeks">
    <div><div class="big">1</div><h3>Play</h3><span class="lbl">↓ Week 1</span><ul><li>Explore the factory kits</li><li>Mute, Note Repeat, Full Level</li><li>Record 3 two-bar beats</li><li>Learn Undo and Erase</li></ul></div>
    <div><div class="big">2</div><h3>Sample</h3><span class="lbl">↓ Week 2</span><ul><li>10 sounds from home and street</li><li>A record or instrument via Line In</li><li>Chop in all three modes</li><li>Build and save your own kit</li></ul></div>
    <div><div class="big">3</div><h3>Transform</h3><span class="lbl">↓ Week 3</span><ul><li>Pad FX and Flex Beat live</li><li>Knob FX on a bassline</li><li>16 Levels for a melody</li><li>Resample an idea</li></ul></div>
    <div><div class="big">4</div><h3>Finish</h3><span class="lbl">↓ Week 4</span><ul><li>3 sequences: intro, A, B</li><li>Perform the arrangement live</li><li>A 60–90 second piece</li><li>Share it with someone</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="ideas"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">8.0</div><h2>Out of the box<span>Design + code</span></h2><p class="intro">For a designer, the MPC is also a tool for identity, prototyping and experiences. Six starting points.</p></div>
  <div class="ideas">
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.1</span><span>Code</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_LAPTOP}}</div><h3>Pads that draw</h3><p>MIDI Out triggers shapes, colors or type in a p5.js, TouchDesigner or Three.js sketch. A visual instrument for presentations.</p><p class="how">MIDI Out → adapter → USB interface → Web MIDI</p></article>
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.2</span><span>Identity</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_TYPE}}</div><h3>Rhythmic type</h3><p>A brand name of up to 16 letters fits a 16-step sequence. One sound per letter: the name heard as rhythm, a starting point for a sonic logo.</p><p class="how">1 letter = 1 step · vowels = notes</p></article>
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.3</span><span>Studio</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_TOOLS}}</div><h3>The studio as a kit</h3><p>Sample the tools of the trade: pen, X-Acto, keyboard, Riso, tearing paper. A drum kit made of design.</p><p class="how">Built-in mic · Chop by Threshold</p></article>
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.4</span><span>Lisbon</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_PHONE}}</div><h3>Sound diary</h3><p>Streetcars, gulls, cobblestones, the market, the river. One beat per neighborhood, sent to the New York team as a sonic postcard.</p><p class="how">~5 h battery · name by place</p></article>
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.5</span><span>Product</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_SPEAKER}}</div><h3>Interface sounds</h3><p>Tap, success, error, notification. A coherent sound family, like a design system for the ear.</p><p class="how">Save Sample → WAV → code prototype</p></article>
    <article class="idea"><div class="tagrow lbl"><span><span class="dot"></span>8.6</span><span>Space</span></div><div class="tile">{{ICON_VINYL}}</div><h3>Synced installation</h3><p>Sync Out sends the tempo pulse to an Arduino: lights, servos or slides on the beat.</p><p class="how">Sync Out → Arduino → 1 pulse = 1 beat</p></article>
  </div>

  <div class="code">
    <div class="head"><span class="lbl">↓ 8.1 in code</span><h3>Pads that draw</h3><p>In Chrome, this listens to any MIDI controller and calls a draw function on every pad hit. Note numbers depend on your setup; <code>console.log</code> shows them.</p></div>
<pre><span class="k">const</span> shapes = {};          <span class="c">// note → shape</span>
navigator.<span class="k">requestMIDIAccess</span>().then(midi =&gt; {
  <span class="k">for</span> (<span class="k">const</span> input <span class="k">of</span> midi.inputs.values()) {
    input.onmidimessage = ({ data: [status, note, vel] }) =&gt; {
      <span class="k">if</span> ((status &amp; 0xf0) === 0x90 &amp;&amp; vel &gt; 0) {
        console.log(<span class="s">'pad'</span>, note, vel);
        draw(note, vel / 127);   <span class="c">// velocity = scale, opacity…</span>
      }
    };
  }
});</pre>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="shortcuts"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="shead"><div class="no">9.0</div><h2>Shortcuts<span>and glossary</span></h2><p class="intro">The <span class="key">SHIFT</span> combos, as printed on the panel.</p></div>
  <div class="cheat">
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">SAMPLE</span></span><span>Input Config</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">SEQ</span></span><span>Step Edit</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key fx">PAD FX</span></span><span>Flex Beat</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key fx">KNOB FX</span></span><span>FX Select</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">ERASE</span></span><span>Copy</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">NOTE REPEAT</span></span><span>Triplet</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pp">CHOP</span></span><span>Note On: sounds only while held</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pp">MUTE</span></span><span>Unmute All</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pp">LOOP</span></span><span>Reverse</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pp">16 LEVELS</span></span><span>Type</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">TAP TEMPO</span></span><span>Metronome</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">SMP SELECT</span></span><span>Save Sample</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">−</span> / <span class="key">+</span></span><span>Undo / Redo</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key rec">SEQ REC</span> <span class="key rec">SMP REC</span></span><span>Recall</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key">▶</span></span><span>Continue</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pad">PAD 1</span></span><span>Full Level</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pad">PAD 2</span> <span class="key pad">3</span></span><span>Half Seq · Double Seq</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pad">PAD 4</span></span><span>Count-in</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key sh">SHIFT</span> <span class="key pad">PAD 9</span></span><span>Fader parameter</span></div>
    <div><span><span class="key">ERASE</span> + pad</span><span>Delete that pad’s notes</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="shead" style="margin-bottom:24px"><div class="no">9.1</div><h2>Glossary</h2></div>
  <dl class="gloss">
    <div><dt>Chop</dt><dd>Cutting a sample into slices, each on its own pad.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Overdub</dt><dd>Recording on top of what’s there without erasing it.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Quantize</dt><dd>Snapping notes to the nearest grid line.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Threshold</dt><dd>The level at which something happens.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Resample</dt><dd>Recording the MPC’s own output as a new sample.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Aftertouch</dt><dd>Pressure after the hit; the pad keeps listening to your finger.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Note On</dt><dd>The sound plays only while you hold the pad.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Timestretch</dt><dd>Changing length without changing pitch. Use sparingly.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</div></section>
</main>

